  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Agenda - Regional Eastern Europe (SEI) - Green Transition - Regional Eastern Europe</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Gr&#xf6;n Agenda - Regional &#xd6;steuropa (SEI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Background: Armenia, Georgia, Moldova, and Ukraine are facing similar environmental, energy, and climate challenges which require urgent actions.&#xa0;The four target countries all cooperate in the Eastern Partnership framework and have association/partnership agreements with EU, which commit them to harmonize (to different extent) their environmental standards with EU&apos;s.&#xa0;In June 2022 the EU granted candidate status to Ukraine and Moldova. However, so far climate and environment have not been given the attention needed by governments in order to face the global and regional challenges.

This project aims to support an increased understanding among partners of EU requirements and the potential gains of strengthened strategic planning for reaching the EU Green Deal targets. This would enable, over time, countries to mobilize increased financial support from EU and other donors/financers and hence scale-up needed investments.&#xa0;Importantly, the project approach is to build capacities by complementing and building on current support in the sector and facilitate a strengthened sector and donor coordination.

The project will support:

- a comprehensivel assessment of the state of affairs in environment, climate, energy and other EU Green Deal related areas in Armenia, Georgia, Moldova, and Ukraine. The assessment will cover institutional, legal and policy gaps in relation to the EU Green Deal Acquis;

- development of country-specific roadmaps, which are specific to the Green Deal and are based on the implementation gaps/challenges (as in the item above). During implementation there would be opportunities for a number of experience sharing events between countries;

- development of priority project proposals for financing by EU and other donors/IFI in the coming years;

- preparation of a &quot;Green deal declaration&quot; (if wanted by countries)&#xa0;for Georgia, Moldova, Ukraine, and possibly Armenia, confirming the commitment of the countries to&#xa0;EU values and principles and the vision of a stable and united Europe;

- the implementation of Roadmaps through technical assistance and capacity building. The more costly parts of the roadmap implementation would follow after the project&apos;s life span but the project have some resources (within Work Package 5) to address less costly priority gaps (e g legal drafting).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bakgrund: Armenien, Georgien, Moldavien och Ukraina &#xe4;r har liknande milj&#xf6;-, energi- och klimatutmaningar vilka kr&#xe4;ver br&#xe5;dskande &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder.&#xa0;De fyra l&#xe4;nderna samarbetar alla inom ramen f&#xf6;r det &#xd6;stliga Partnerskapet och har associerings-/partnerskapsavtal med EU, vilka f&#xf6;rbinder dem att (i olika utstr&#xe4;ckning) harmonisera sina milj&#xf6;standarder med EU:s.&#xa0;&#xa0;I juni 2022 beviljade EU Ukraina och Moldavien kandidatstatus. Hittills har dock regeringarna inte prioriterat klimat och milj&#xf6; i den utstr&#xe4;ckning som beh&#xf6;vs f&#xf6;r att m&#xf6;ta de globala och regionala utmaningarna.

Projekt syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja en &#xf6;kad f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else hos partners f&#xf6;r EU:s krav och de potentiella vinsterna med att mer strategiskt planera f&#xf6;r ett n&#xe4;rmande till EU:s gr&#xf6;na giv. Detta skulle bl a g&#xf6;ra det m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r l&#xe4;nderna att mobilisera ett &#xf6;kat ekonomiskt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n EU och andra givare/finansi&#xe4;rer och d&#xe4;rmed kunna &#xf6;ka takten i milj&#xf6;omst&#xe4;llningen. Projektets ansats &#xe4;r att bygga kapacitet genom att komplettera och bygga vidare p&#xe5; det nuvarande st&#xf6;det i sektorn samt underl&#xe4;tta en f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt sektor- och givarsamordning.

Projektet avser att st&#xf6;dja:

- En omfattande bed&#xf6;mning och analys av situationen inom milj&#xf6;, klimat, energi och andra omr&#xe5;den med anknytning till EU:s gr&#xf6;na giv i Armenien, Georgien, Moldavien och Ukraina. Bed&#xf6;mningen kommer att omfatta institutionella, r&#xe4;ttsliga och politiska &quot;luckor&quot; i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till EU:s regelverk (de delar som &#xe4;r relevanta f&#xf6;r den gr&#xf6;na given).

&#x2013; Framtagande av landsanpassade f&#xe4;rdplaner som &#xe4;r specifika f&#xf6;r den gr&#xf6;na given och som bygger p&#xe5; bed&#xf6;mningen/&quot;gap analysis&quot; ovan. Under genomf&#xf6;randet planeras ett antal evenemang f&#xf6;r erfarenhetsutbyte mellan l&#xe4;nderna.

- Utveckling av ett antal prioriterade projektf&#xf6;rslag f&#xf6;r m&#xf6;jlig finansiering av EU och bilaterala givare under de kommande &#xe5;ren.

&#x2013; Utarbetande av en f&#xf6;rklaring/&quot;declaration&quot; om den gr&#xf6;na given (om l&#xe4;nderna s&#xe5; &#xf6;nskar) f&#xf6;r Georgien, Moldavien, Ukraina och eventuellt Armenien, som bekr&#xe4;ftar l&#xe4;ndernas engagemang f&#xf6;r EU:s v&#xe4;rderingar och principer och visionen om ett stabilt och enat Europa.

- Genomf&#xf6;rande av delar av f&#xe4;rdplanerna genom tekniskt bist&#xe5;nd och kapacitetsuppbyggnad. De mer kostsamma delarna av f&#xe4;rdplanerna f&#xf6;ljer efter projektets livsl&#xe4;ngd men projektet har vissa resurser (inom arbetspaket 5) f&#xf6;r mindre kostsamma prioriteringar (t ex behov av ny lagstiftning).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the extension phase, the Green Agenda will be implemented by SEI in Armenia, Moldova and Ukraine.

The overall objective is an inclusive, sustainable and efficient pathway towards green and just transition in Armenia, Moldova and Ukraine aligned with EU policy objectives and EU accession criteria.

The intermediate outcomes are:

1. The Governments of Armenia, Moldova, and Ukraine are adopting and implementing green transition plans and environmental policies aligned with EU Environment and Climate policies and EU accession criteria. 

2. Civil society and the general public in Armenia, Moldova, and Ukraine are engaged in the green and just transition

3. Governments of Armenia, Moldova, and Ukraine are sharing experiences and tools to address common green transition challenges. 

The project has the following immediate outcomes:

1. Governments of Armenia, Moldova, and Ukraine have improved skills, tools, and clear pathways to develop HRBA-based, EU-aligned sectoral green transition roadmaps/plans. 

2. Governments of Armenia, Moldova, and Ukraine have increased capacity to implement decarbonization projects, enabling inclusive green jobs and a just transition. 

3. Increased awareness, understanding, and acceptance of sustainability and just transition among civil society and the broader public 

4. Improved conditions for regional cooperation and increased opportunities to share green and just transition practices</narrative>
  </description>
